      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "As $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left, the function $g(x)$ approaches $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=2.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the right, the function $g(x)$ approaches $0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=0.\n$$",
